%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S10 + D26 + D43 + D44
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant TEL as Telephony
    participant MG as Media gateway
    participant STT as STT workers
    participant WS as Workstation
    participant A as Agent

    TEL->>TEL: caller leg and agent leg are BRIDGED
    Note over TEL,MG: each leg is forked SEPARATELY (D26)<br/>so we never need speaker diarisation -<br/>we know which wire the audio came from

    par caller audio
        TEL->>MG: fork of the caller leg
        MG->>STT: 20ms frames, VAD-segmented
        STT-->>WS: turns tagged speaker=customer
    and agent audio
        TEL->>MG: fork of the agent leg
        MG->>STT: same pipeline
        STT-->>WS: turns tagged speaker=agent
    end

    WS->>A: live transcript, both sides, colour-coded

    Note over A,C: the keypad stays live all call (D43/D44)
    A->>C: asks for a number they actually have
    A->>WS: START capture
    C->>TEL: keys the digits
    TEL->>WS: digits as they arrive
    A->>WS: STOP capture
    Note right of WS: capture is UNTYPED - we did not<br/>assume WHICH document they hold

    alt agent runs an optional lookup
        A->>WS: match against this customer's policies
        WS-->>A: matched MT-2025-004512
        Note right of WS: EVIDENCE ONLY. Changes no assurance.
    else agent just uses the digits
        WS-->>A: the digits, and nothing else happens
    end

    A->>WS: attests - Confirmed / Not this person / Third party (D42)
    WS->>WS: assurance updated, brief re-renders as v2
    Note right of WS: a match cannot tell the policyholder from<br/>a daughter holding his documents. Only a<br/>human can make that call.

    A->>WS: presses Hang up
    WS->>TEL: end the call
